lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record here runs from 1951 to 2025, and February to March came in under 90% of normal in 36 of those 75 years on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids. In 2025 the middle of the grids got 140% of normal in September to October and 47% in November to December. So far in 2026, February to March sits at 44% of normal on the middle of the grids. Every grid had its driest year in 2007, with grids 18472 and 18473 down at 64%.</p>"}
